    "q-102700": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102700",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,2,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}\\text{ }i-{e}^{z}\\text{ }j-y{e}^{z}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2,1) & =\\frac{2}{1}\\text{ }i-{e}^{1}\\text{ }j-(2){e}^{1}k \\\\  & =2\\,i-e\\,j-2ek \\\\  & =⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
